            "review_title": "Review at The Friend Restaurant",
            "review_text": "Brodie M\n9 contributions\n1\nTrue to their name\nJun 2019 • Couples\nThis new restaurant in District 7 offers up some good food at good prices. We went for lunch and had pasta with a meatball and homemade tomato sauce (60.000) and Spaghetti carbonara (50.000). Both meals were good, and the grated cheese shaker on the table was a nice touch. The restaurant just opened this week, so they are still working some kinks out, but the owners (a Vietnamese-American couple) were friendly and eager to please. For dessert we had creme brulee (tasty!) and French-style rice pudding (rich and creamy). The desserts were 30k each. They also offer American-style breakfasts including omelettes, pancakes, and bacon. Several varieties of beer are available including Hoegaarden and Corona. We haven't tried the pizza yet, but this is probably your only option for a slice in this neighborhood.\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nReview collected in partnership with this restaurant \nWritten June 12, 2019\nNhư Ngân\nThank you for your review. Hope you guys are having a very good trip in Vietnam.\nWritten August 7, 2019\nThis response is the subjective opinion of the management representative and not of Tripadvisor LLC nor of its partners.",
